WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.917
(bright swing music)

00:00:01.917 --> 00:00:03.834
- If there's one thing that
we New Yorkers hold dear,

00:00:03.834 --> 00:00:05.220
it's our bagels.

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:08.170
But I live in LA now and
the bagels aren't horrible.

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:10.180
So what is it about a New York bagel?

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:12.350
Are they really that much
better than LA bagels?

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:13.342
Is it the recipe?

00:00:13.342 --> 00:00:14.270
The water?

00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:16.270
Is it just plain nostalgia?

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:18.610
Well I came to the Bagel
Broker in LA to find out.

00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:22.060
(big band like music)

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:24.200
What specific qualities should someone

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.320
look for in a great bagel?

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:28.910
- The first experience
should be a nice, good crunch

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:30.290
and it should get softer and softer

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:31.910
as you get to the middle of the bagel.

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:33.942
And the ingredients and the flavor

00:00:33.942 --> 00:00:36.420
is a big thing that you gotta work with.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:39.460
- A lot of people would
say that LA bagels,

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:41.170
not as good as New York bagels.

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:43.542
- That would be a statement
made by New Yorkers

00:00:43.542 --> 00:00:45.550
but I think it's just been
ingrained in New Yorkers' heads

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:49.001
from when they were children
that bagels are New York

00:00:49.001 --> 00:00:50.810
and pizza is New York.

00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:52.470
Nothing compares.

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:53.270
- To test this theory

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:54.560
I need to get six bagels

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:56.850
I picked up LA bagels
from the Bagel Broker,

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:59.690
Noah's New York Bagels, and Sam's Bagels.

00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:00.940
Got the last of the LA Bagels.

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:04.812
Then I had bagels shipped
from my childhood bagel place,

00:01:04.812 --> 00:01:06.650
Bagel Boss, in New York.

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:08.561
Now, six New Yorkers are going to see

00:01:08.561 --> 00:01:11.160
if they can choose the New York Bagel.

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:15.830
- What are we looking at here?

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:17.830
- That, aesthetically,
is very pleasing to me

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:20.822
but I realize it's just
melted cheese on top.

00:01:20.822 --> 00:01:23.840
- Flat. Kind of a weird texture.

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:26.330
- There should be a very tiny hole here,

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:28.000
but the fact that I can
see through both of these

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.430
like eye goggles, not good.

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:30.470
Not a New York bagel.

00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:31.540
- Oh, you can smell the
jalapenos in this one.

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:32.560
- Yeah it's pretty

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:34.922
- I like a lot of cream
cheese on my bagels.

00:01:34.922 --> 00:01:35.890
- Me too. My grandma like,

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:38.600
"That's a nice, healthy
schmear of cream cheese."

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:40.860
- This has LA bagel written all over it.

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:43.280
- I mean, I'm eating it,
but it's not that great.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:44.900
- It's edible, but it's not New York.

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:46.400
- Agreed. 100% agreed.

00:01:47.510 --> 00:01:49.070
Ok.

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:51.660
What?

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:52.940
So these are shriveled.

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:56.040
- Are these cranberries
and rye seeds or something?

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:57.620
- The hole here

00:01:57.620 --> 00:01:59.460
is a little bit smaller.
- Ah there we go!

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:01.960
- See, I can't really put my
finger through it that time.

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:03.420
- It seems like the New
York bagel is something that

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:05.760
like, really can't be
bleeped with, you know?

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.300
I don't know that
they're about introducing

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:08.840
new, kooky flavors.

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:11.680
- Oh my God, even trying
to rip it apart is awful.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:13.510
- It feels cold and sad.

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:15.520
- I feel cold in my bleeping soul.

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:17.480
- Do you think it's a New York bagel?

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:18.520
- Oh man, I don't know.

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:21.060
I feel like I have to taste
all of them and then decide.

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:21.722
- I know.

00:02:21.722 --> 00:02:22.900
- These seem very LA to me.

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:24.900
- You can just look at it and
know that it was made in LA.

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:26.480
- I don't think this is a New York bagel.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:28.150
- Why're you eating more of it?

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:29.030
- I don't, because I'm upset.

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:36.900
- This is an egg bagel
and this is definitely

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:39.040
a New York bleeping bagel.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:39.750
- What?

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:42.250
- What is that?

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:45.781
- See how, see how wide this is?

00:02:45.781 --> 00:02:46.832
This is what a New York bagel is.

00:02:46.832 --> 00:02:48.912
- These raisins are weird.

00:02:48.912 --> 00:02:51.890
- It's got that fluffy feel to it.

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:53.543
You can smell it from afar.

00:02:53.543 --> 00:02:55.220
- Different colored raisins? I don't know.

00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:58.132
- This reminds me of
breaking fast at Yom Kippur.

00:02:58.132 --> 00:02:59.480
- It's better.
- It's better.

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:01.470
- The flavor of the seeds are definitely

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:03.440
coming through after as an after taste.

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:05.352
- That actually tastes pretty good though.

00:03:05.352 --> 00:03:06.350
- There's a density.

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:07.012
- It's alive.

00:03:07.012 --> 00:03:08.530
- I'm choking up it's so good.

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:10.933
- I'm gonna wing towards New York.

00:03:10.933 --> 00:03:11.950
- I don't know
- Weird

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:14.530
- The raisins alone will
make me say no, it's from LA.

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:17.080
- I'm not ready to say that
this is from New York though.

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:19.450
- That makes me homesick for New York.

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:21.902
I miss New York really badly.

00:03:24.622 --> 00:03:26.960
- This one looks promising.

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:28.550
- I'm suddenly doubting
everything I said about

00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:29.660
the other bagels.

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:30.910
- This is it, I can just
feel my tongue tingling.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:31.630
- Together.

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:32.190
- Look at that.

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:33.020
- Together.

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:34.800
- Those raisins look normal.

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:35.960
- And I like the swirl.

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:39.140
- Size, look at that, squishiness.

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:40.310
- See, small holes.

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:42.180
- There's like no comparison.

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:44.230
- It's got the look, it's got the feel,

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:46.190
there's something just a little bit off

00:03:46.190 --> 00:03:47.690
that I can't put my finger on.

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:51.440
- None of these are really,
like, jumping out at me

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:53.410
as the bagel of my childhood.

00:03:53.410 --> 00:03:54.860
- I really thought that the one before was

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:55.660
the New York bagel.

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:57.910
But this could be a
New York bagel as well.

00:03:57.910 --> 00:03:59.570
But it might be an impostor.

00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:01.080
- What I'm saying is that the last bagel

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:02.530
is a New York bagel.

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:04.660
- This swirl is telling me something.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:07.500
I'm gonna have to go
with the last one too.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:08.840
- Number three.

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:09.782
- Yeah I go with Zo with three.

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:11.010
Three is a New York bagel.

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:12.970
- I'm going with three.
Please tell me I'm right.

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:17.530
- I'm nervous. I'm nervous.

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:19.350
- Bleep.

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:22.360
- Whaaaat?

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:27.900
- Yes!

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.480
- Oh my God, I'm so happy!

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:30.480
- Really?

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:31.780
- My grandmother is
turning over in her grave.

00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:33.700
- What happened to it in travel, man?

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:35.200
- LA bagels just aren't the same.

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:37.240
When you're eating a New
York bagel you just know.

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:37.820
- Mhm.

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:38.830
- You just know.

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:42.330
(bright, happy jig music)

